Open Database Connectivity 
(Open Control Panel in Classic view and click Administrative Tools, Double-click ODBC Data Sources ,The ODBC Data Source Administrator box opens)
(To make the data source apply to all users of the system, click the System DSN tab , Click Add , The Create New Data Source box appears ,Scroll down to and select SQL Server and 
click Finish. Follow directions on screen to enter the name of the SQL Server computer on the network and the sign-in ID and password to SQL Server ,The database administrator in your organization can 
supply this information)
(If you don’t see the driver you need in the Create New Data Source box, close all windows and use Explorer to locate the C:\Windows\SysWOW64\Odbcad32.exe program file)
